.TH RECVMSG 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
recvmsg \- receive a scatter/gather socket message
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.B ssize_t recvmsg(int descriptor, struct msghdr* message, int flags);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Receives data into the writable iovec buffers in message.
Linux updates the supplied message header, including address, control lengths
and message flags. Crunch structures use the Linux x86\-64 kernel layout.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns bytes received, possibly fewer than requested, or \-1 with errno set.
Zero can indicate end of stream. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recvfrom (3crunch),
.BR recvmsg (2)
